    "_": "These are used to transform the values coming from physical devices.",
    "_": "This is done at the physical level because a later device mapped to the same",
    "_": "logical device variable may need a different transform, or not need one.",
    "physical_device_templates": [
      {
        "name": "Wombat ATM41",
        "variables": {
          "8_rh": {
            "transform": "value * 100.0"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "_": "This may be redundant. It is meant to be a template describing the variables for a type of device",
    "_": "But it may be just as easy to put the variable types in the variable mappings, which is all this",
    "_": "template does ATM.",
